    "\n",
    "#### Predictions and Residuals\n",
    "\n",
    "Predictions use the parameters calculated in Section 9.1:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\hat{y}_i = w x_i + b\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Here, \\(x_i\\) is standardized median income.\n",
    "\n",
    "A residual is the observed value minus the predicted value:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "e_i = y_i - \\hat{y}_i\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "- Positive residual: the model underestimates the observed value.\n",
    "- Negative residual: the model overestimates the observed value.\n",
    "- A residual near zero indicates a prediction close to the observation.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Mean Squared Error\n",
    "\n",
    "We summarize the training residuals using:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "MSE = \\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(y_i-\\hat{y}_i)^2\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "MSE uses all training observations and is expressed in squared\n",
    "target units. It is not the average error in dollars.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is training error, not an estimate of performance on unseen data.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Plot Design\n",
