    "### 9.3 Gradient-Descent Training\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Purpose\n",
    "\n",
    "Estimate the slope and intercept iteratively, following the professor's\n",
    "manual gradient-descent implementation.\n",
    "\n",
    "The Normal Equation calculates the parameters directly. Gradient descent\n",
    "starts with initial parameters and repeatedly updates them to reduce\n",
    "the training Mean Squared Error (MSE).\n",
    "\n",
    "Both methods use the same standardized training predictor and the same\n",
    "training targets, making their results directly comparable.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Initialization and Predictions\n",
    "\n",
    "We initialize both parameters at zero:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "w = 0,\\qquad b = 0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "At each epoch, predictions are calculated as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\hat{y}_i = w x_i + b\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Here, \\(x_i\\) is standardized median income.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Gradients and Parameter Updates\n",
    "\n",
    "For the full MSE objective, the gradients are:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial MSE}{\\partial w}\n",
    "= -\\frac{2}{n}\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(y_i-\\hat{y}_i)x_i\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{\\partial MSE}{\\partial b}\n",
    "= -\\frac{2}{n}\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(y_i-\\hat{y}_i)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "We update the parameters in the opposite direction of the gradients:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "w \\leftarrow w-\\alpha\\frac{\\partial MSE}{\\partial w}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "b \\leftarrow b-\\alpha\\frac{\\partial MSE}{\\partial b}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Both gradients are calculated using the same predictions before either\n",
    "parameter is updated.\n",
    "\n",
    "Every epoch uses all training observations. This is batch gradient descent.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Training Settings\n",
    "\n",
    "- Learning rate: `0.01`.\n",
    "- Epochs: `2000`.\n",
    "- Initial slope and intercept: `0.0`.\n",
    "- Predictor: standardized median income.\n",
    "- Target: median house value in its original units.\n",
    "\n",
    "The learning rate controls the size of each update.\n",
    "An epoch here corresponds to one update using the full training set.\n",
    "\n",
    "We retain the professor's loop and 2,000 epochs, but use a learning rate\n",
    "appropriate for our standardized predictor rather than copying `1e-8`\n",
    "from the house-size example.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Recording Training Progress\n",
    "\n",
    "We record MSE after each parameter update. Therefore, the last entry in\n",
    "`loss_history` corresponds to the final fitted parameters.\n",
    "\n",
    "This differs slightly from recording the pre-update predictions:\n",
    "it aligns the reported final error with the reported final coefficients.\n",
    "\n",
    "Training uses no test observations. Agreement with the Normal Equation\n",
    "will indicate convergence to the same least-squares solution, not\n",
    "perfect prediction accuracy."
   ]
  },
