    "### 9.5 Compare Analytical and Gradient-Descent Lines\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Purpose\n",
    "\n",
    "Compare the regression lines obtained through two different\n",
    "parameter-estimation methods:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Normal Equation: a direct analytical calculation.\n",
    "2. Gradient descent: iterative parameter updates.\n",
    "\n",
    "Both methods minimize the same training Mean Squared Error.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Fair Comparison\n",
    "\n",
    "Both models use:\n",
    "\n",
    "- The same training observations.\n",
    "- The same standardized median-income predictor.\n",
    "- The same median-house-value target.\n",
    "- One slope and one intercept.\n",
    "\n",
    "No models are refitted in this section.\n",
    "We reuse the parameters calculated in Sections 9.1 and 9.3.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Plot Design\n",
    "\n",
    "Following the professor's comparison:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Blue points show the training observations.\n",
